  "claim": "The historical 2026-10-04 foundation E2E covered 15 units and 80 slots through native executor observations, independent model review and 22 adjudications. Final labels are READY 18, PARTIAL 31, FAIL 2, BY_DESIGN 12 and INTERIM 17, with zero unjudged slots. Readiness is (18 + 12) / 80 = 37.5%, rounded half up to 38%; all 22 executor/reviewer disagreements were adjudicated. This publication independently checks and sanitizes the retained status chains; it does not repeat host or provider execution. Missing prompt, adjudicator model metadata and separate fix-list provenance are explicit.",
  "limitations": [
    "Host state is as of 2026-10-04 19:10–20:10Z only; later source merge timestamp 2026-10-04T20:26:16Z does not extend that observation window. No commands were run on any WSL distribution by this publisher.",
    "Fixes are pending. The 33 PARTIAL/FAIL slots after adjudication are not accepted as ready: 25 repository-plan and 8 host fixes (evidence/artifacts/ns2604-e2e-20261004/fixes.json); six token slots resolve with PR #684.",
    "This is not an upstream benchmark. Native executor observations, independent model judgments and adjudication are separate from upstream tests, structural checks, independent host replication and measured quality or token improvement.",
    "The 17 INTERIM slots are held by design. They remain in the denominator and contribute zero to the readiness numerator; the 12 BY_DESIGN slots are intentional dispositions rather than proof that their tools executed.",
    "Adjudication: Claude Opus 5.5 at effort max (evidence-reviewer), prompt template in evidence/artifacts/ns2604-e2e-20261004/adjudication-prompt.md; separate adjudication start/end timestamps are not retained.",
    "Historical source command excerpts and raw conversations remain private. Public reasons are bounded to 60 words, fixes preserve the merge's 900-character bound before sanitization, and citations are limited to four per slot. Hashes establish byte identity, not success or adequacy of every native acceptance claim.",
    "Reviewer records report the requested gateway model cx/gpt-6.1-sol-max and max effort; no resolved backend model identity is inferred. Independent model review is review of retained evidence, not independent execution on the host.",
    "The publisher leaves the receipt and new artifact hashes unregistered for the coordinator-owned manifests/evidence.json. Full repository validation is expected to report registry drift until integration; per-file scans and local receipt tests are structural evidence only."
  ],
